# Fused whole-struct internal read other than per field (list-length) — refused

The FUSION (PHASE5C-TUTORIAL §3a, 2026-08-25) inlines a whole-struct per-element
map INTERNAL — `map each g among source to (output of Callee with {…})` — ONLY
where it is consumed as a bare per-field read (`map each x among shares to
x.field`): the struct list never exists on the wire. Here `shares` IS consumed
per field (the `totaal` fold), but ALSO read whole by `number of shares` (a
list-length). That non-per-field read has no per-field image — the fused list is
not on the wire — so it refuses loudly (Direction B), rather than crashing on the
absent `vars` entry (the lens flank: a fused internal is excluded from `vars`).

```catala
declaration scope Kamer:
  input grondslag content integer
  output bedrag content integer

scope Kamer:
  definition bedrag equals grondslag + 100

declaration scope Aanslag:
  input grondslagen content list of integer
  internal shares content list of Kamer
  output totaal content integer
  output aantal content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition shares equals
    map each g among grondslagen to
    (output of Kamer with { -- grondslag: g })
  definition totaal equals
    sum integer of map each s among shares to s.bedrag
  definition aantal equals number of shares
```
